{v_1: list(str)} |= ∀i ∈ [0, v_1.len - 1] : v_1[i] = "relu" ∨ v_1[i] = "tanh" ∨ v_1[i] = "sigmoid" ∨ v_1[i] = "softmax" ∨ v_1[i] = "elu" ∨ v_1[i] = "selu" ∨ v_1[i] = "gelu" ∨ v_1[i] = "swish" ∨ v_1[i] = "softplus" ∨ v_1[i] = "linear"
>>
Rule 143 (if two tensors shapes is same for certain dimension then dtype value should be also same.)
{v_1: tensor, v_2: tensor} |= if ∃i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) = shape(v_2, i) then dtype_(v_1) = dtype_(v_2)
>>
Rule 144 (if the value is a tuple of int. at least two number should be same)
{v_1: tuple(int)} |= if v_1.len > 1 then ∃i ∈ [0, v_1.len - 1] : ∃j ∈ [i+1, v_1.len -1] : v_1[i] = v_1[j]
>>
Rule 145 (If String has the interpolation value nearest it must have three dimensions)
{v_1: str, v_2: tensor} |= if v_1 = "nearest" then ndim(v_2) = 3
>>
Rule 146 (if there is a float and the float should be in the range (1e-5, 1e5))
{v_1: float} |= v_1 > 0.00001 ∧ v_1 < 100000
>>
Rule 149 (The shape can be either 1D or 2D but not more than that)
{v_1: tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = 1 ∨ ndim(v_1) = 2
>>
Rule 150 (if there are two tensors and the first dimension of 1st array and last dimension must be less than last shape and 1st shape)
{v_1: tensor, v_2: tensor} |= shape(v_1,0) < shape(v_2, ndim(v_2)-1) ∧ shape(v_1, ndim(v_1)-1) < shape(v_2,0)
